description:
The Policy & Research Group (PRG) specializes in research and evaluation of public policy and programs in the following areas: education, public health, child welfare, workforce and income, housing, juvenile justice, and adolescent risk reduction. PRG aims to improve the economic and social prospects for all people through equitable public policy and improved practice. Our mission is to produce rigorous research and evaluation that benefits people by improving programs and innovations that aim to improve social, behavioral, health, economic, and employment potential. As a small but expanding research and evaluation firm, PRG operates a casual work environment that is both professionally and intellectually demanding, allows employees at all levels to play an integral role in projects, and provides opportunities for growth. PRG is an employee-owned small business. See www.policyandresearch.com for more information.

PRG is seeking a motivated, detail-oriented Junior Research Analyst to support the development, maintenance, and monitoring of data management systems used in research and evaluation projects. This is a full-time, exempt position within PRG's Data Management Team. The successful candidate will work under the guidance of experienced technical staff to maintain automated data processing workflows, develop and troubleshoot data dashboards, conduct data quality checks, and support other technical data management activities. PRG will provide training in its specific systems, tools, and procedures, with opportunities to develop technical skills and assume greater responsibility over time.

The ideal candidate will have foundational programming skills, particularly in Python or SQL, strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, and an interest in developing technical data management expertise. Experience with Stata, JavaScript, and data visualization platforms is preferred but not required.

**Responsibilities:**

Responsibilities will vary based on project needs, but may include:

* Monitoring and maintaining data dashboards to ensure accurate and timely reporting;
* Assisting with the development, maintenance, and automation of data pipelines and dashboards;
* Identifying, troubleshooting, and resolving technical issues with data pipelines, dashboards, and automated processes;
* Responding to help desk requests from users of data dashboards and related systems;
* Developing and maintaining data management scripts, including Stata .do files, Python scripts, and SQL queries;
* Performing routine data quality checks and validation procedures to ensure accuracy and consistency in reporting;
* Reviewing variable definitions, codebooks, and data management scripts to ensure consistency with established procedures;
* Documenting data management processes, technical procedures, and system updates;
* Collaborating with project teams to support data management, monitoring, and reporting activities.

**Qualifications:**

* Bachelor's degree in computer science, data science, information systems, or a closely related technical field;
* Demonstrated programming proficiency, particularly in Python and/or SQL, through coursework, internships, employment, or independent projects;
* Strong analytical, critical thinking, and technical problem-solving skills;
* Exceptional attention to detail and commitment to accuracy;
* Strong communication and organizational skills, including the ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines;
* Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team;
* Self-motivated, with a willingness to learn new technologies and technical procedures;
* Commitment to PRG's mission of improving programs and policies through rigorous research and evaluation.

Candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas are preferred:

* Experience programming in Stata and/or JavaScript;
* Experience developing or maintaining data dashboards using Cluvio, Power BI, Tableau, or similar platforms;
* Experience developing automated data pipelines and data processing workflows;
* Experience in data management and data validation;
* Experience working with web content management systems such as WordPress;
* Experience using Git or other version control systems for collaborative code development;
* Familiarity with data privacy and security standards, including HIPAA and FERPA.

**Benefits:**

* Two weeks (10 days) paid vacation per year, with increase to three weeks after one year of employment
* Approximately 17 paid holidays per year (this includes an end of the year break where the office is closed between Christmas and New Year’s Day)
* Medical, dental, and vision group plans offered; employer pays portion of premiums
* Supplemental insurance plans and a Flexible Spending Account (FSA) offered
* After two years of employment, PRG employees are eligible to contribute to SIMPLE and Roth IRA retirement plans with employer percentage match.

**Starting Salary:** $50,000

**Location and Working Hours:** This is a remote position open to candidates anywhere in the U.S., with office space available for individuals based in New Orleans, LA. As this position will support a project based in Alaska, the successful candidate must be available to work from 9:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Alaska Time (generally 1:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. Central Time), with occasional evening or weekend hours as needed. Travel for 1–2 in-person meetings per year may be required. Applicants should indicate their preferred work location in their cover letter and state their understanding of the standard working hours for this position.

**Position Start Date:** The anticipated start date for this position is December 2026.

**To Apply:** Please submit a cover letter, resume, application form, unofficial transcripts, and three references via the application section accessible in the following link: https://policyandresearch.bamboohr.com/careers/34?source=aWQ9MjA%3D

**Equal Opportunity:** PRG is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and we do not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, sex, age, national origin, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability. We welcome all candidates to consider joining our team.

Job Type: Full-time

Pay: $50,000.00 per year

Benefits:

* 401(k) matching
* Dental insurance
* Flexible spending account
* Health insurance
* Health savings account
* Vision insurance

Work Location: Hybrid remote in New Orleans, LA 70118

The primary responsibility of the Data Analyst is to support the reporting, analytics, and operational data needs of the School Health Clinics of Santa Clara County (SHCSCC). This position is responsible for the development, maintenance, validation, automation, and distribution of reports, dashboards, and data solutions that support clinical operations, regulatory compliance, quality improvement initiatives, financial analysis, and organizational decision-making. The Data Analyst serves as a technical resource for healthcare reporting, business intelligence, and data management utilizing Epic, SQL, Tableau, SSRS, and other reporting technologies. Responsibilities include maintaining reporting infrastructure, supporting automated reporting processes, performing data validation and analysis, supporting supplemental data submissions and regulatory reporting requirements, and ensuring the reliability of critical reporting functions. Working collaboratively with operational, clinical, quality improvement, finance, and leadership teams, the Data Analyst translates business requirements into actionable reporting solutions while identifying opportunities to improve efficiency through automation, process improvement, and data-driven decision support.

Essential Duties and Responsibilities

* Gather, analyze, document, and translate business requirements into reporting, analytics, and data management solutions.
* Develop, maintain, validate, and distribute reports, dashboards, and data extracts using Epic, SQL, SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS), Tableau, Excel, and other reporting tools.
* Support regulatory and compliance reporting requirements including UDS, HCAI, health plan reporting, grant reporting, supplemental data submissions, and other organizational reporting obligations.
* Performs ad-hoc data analysis using tools such as OCHIN Epic Reporting Workbench, OCHIN Epic Clarity, OCHIN Epic Crystal Reports, OCHIN Epic SAP Business Objects, and application analytic packages.
* Provide technical support and troubleshooting for reporting systems, Epic applications, analytics tools, and business system applications.
* Documents issues and resolutions in the user-facing helpdesk knowledgebase system.
* Participates in the planning and execution of the overall business systems roadmap; understanding changing business needs, company objectives, and resource allocation.
* Provides technical support to the end-users on all business system applications.
* Documents issues and resolutions in the user-facing helpdesk knowledge base system.
* Develops positive and collaborative relationships with business stakeholders, technical resources, application users, and corporate management.
* Manages multiple simultaneous projects and tasks with changing priorities.
* Maintains currency of knowledge with respect to relevant state-of-the-art technology, equipment, and/or systems.
* Assists in the enforcement of project deadlines and schedules.
* Contributes to developing organizational functional knowledge.
* Anticipates customer needs and proactively develops solutions to meet them.
* Identifies and executes opportunities to improve process workflows.
* Determines and defines business requirements based on government regulations and business needs.
* Performs OCHIN EHR Support Analyst roles and responsibilities as needed.
* Provides direct support to clinical operation and patient care teams to facilitate the introduction, acceptance, integration, and optimal use of the Epic application in the clinic.
* Provides daily support to application users through troubleshooting, coaching, and consulting.
* Maintains member-managed system setups such as the provider master file, security, and preference lists.
* For EHR support, works collaboratively with clinicians and follows established EMR processes.
* Collaborates with OCHIN to test new features and upgrades prior to implementation.
* Attends appropriate clinic department meetings as Epic expert and as OCHIN liaison.
* Maintains Enterprise Practice setups, including the Clinic Resource, Security rights and user accounts, Definitions, Fee Schedule, and Procedure Code tables.
* Manages user accounts.
* Generates metric reports as needed.

Secondary Responsibilities

* Attends workshops, training, and meetings as needed, and as requested.
* Performs other duties as assigned by the supervisor.
* Works flexible schedule and overtime, as necessary.

QUALIFICATIONS

* Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Information Management, Health Information, Public

Health or related field preferred, or at least 1 year of proven experience;

* Minimum one year working with computer systems related to health care;
* Minimum one year of data analysis experience; focus on health data preferred;
* Proficiency in FQHC-related data reporting, specifically UDS, HEDIS, and Clinical Quality

Measures;

* Proficiency in Excel particularly advanced level;
* Proficiency in SQL;
* Proficiency in other data reporting and development tools such as Tableau, R, SAS, Python,

Business Objects desired but not required.

* Proficiency in other Microsoft Office applications such as Word and PowerPoint;
* Ability to learn new skills related to healthcare;
* Ability to assume sole and independent responsibility for various assigned projects and tasks;
* Ability to exercise discretion and independent judgment with respect to significant matters;
* Strong interpersonal skills
* Strong business acumen and insight into clinical processes;
* Strong organizational, time management skills and attention to detail;
* Strong analytical skills and problem-solving skills with the ability to focus on detail;
* Strong ability to identify potential issues and participate in their resolution;
* Ability to work on several projects and assignments simultaneously;
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
* Ability to complete projects with tight deadlines and time constraints;
* Solid understanding of the implementation process and the various interdependencies between operations and technology;

Pay: From $35.00 per hour

Expected hours: 24.0 per week

Work Location: In person

We are looking for a **Senior Scientist** specializing in Statistical Process Control (SPC) and Data Analytics to support a Global Manufacturing Science & Technology (MSAT) team within the pharmaceutical industry.

This role combines hands-on data preparation, applied statistical analysis, and coding to support manufacturing process monitoring, reporting, and continuous improvement. The ideal candidate is comfortable working with R or Python, preparing and validating datasets, applying statistical methods, and improving analytical workflows. Experience with AI-assisted coding tools is welcome.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* Prepare, clean, merge, validate, and analyze manufacturing and quality datasets using R or Python;
* Apply statistical process control (SPC), control charts, process capability analysis, and comparative statistical methods;
* Monitor process performance, identify trends, investigate statistical alerts, and communicate findings;
* Execute routine and ad hoc analyses and prepare reports and presentations for stakeholders;
* Improve analytical tools, data preparation workflows, and reporting processes through coding and automation;
* Support Continued Process Verification (CPV) and Annual Product Quality Review (APQR) activities;
* Contribute to analytical system configuration, technical documentation, and process improvements;
* Collaborate with MSAT, Manufacturing, Quality, and other cross-functional stakeholders.

**Position details:**

* Hourly rate: $55.80–$60.80;
* Contract length: Initial 6 months with possible extension, subject to client needs and budget approval;
* Location: Madison, NJ 07940 (Giralda Farms);
* Work arrangement: Hybrid, 50% onsite with flexible onsite days;
* Schedule: Monday–Friday, 9 AM–5 PM EST, with core hours of 10 AM–4 PM EST;
* Maximum hours: 40 hours per week;
* Travel: Up to 10% globally;
* W-2 contract position;
* No C2C options;
* No visa sponsorship.


**Requirements**

**Required:**

* Bachelor's degree in Life Sciences, Biotechnology, Engineering, Statistics, Data Science, or a related discipline;
* 5+ years of pharmaceutical experience in a GMP-regulated environment;
* 3+ years of experience in data management and analytics;
* Hands-on coding experience using R or Python for data preparation, manipulation, analysis, or reporting;
* Ability to assess data completeness, identify inconsistencies, and prepare reliable datasets for statistical analysis;
* Practical experience applying statistical methods, including statistical process control (SPC), process monitoring, capability analysis, or comparative statistics;
* Demonstrated project experience applying coding and statistical analysis to real business or technical problems;
* Strong analytical thinking, problem-solving, and technical communication skills;
* Ability to collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders and work effectively within a matrix team;
* Authorization to work in the United States without visa sponsorship.

**Preferred:**

* Experience in pharmaceutical manufacturing, process development, analytical development, or MSAT;
* Experience with Continued Process Verification (CPV) and Annual Product Quality Review (APQR);
* Experience supporting statistical process monitoring in commercial cell therapy or biopharmaceutical manufacturing;
* Experience with JMP, Minitab, or other statistical analysis software;
* Experience with control charts, Shewhart charts, Western Electric rules, t-tests, or Wilcoxon tests;
* Experience with coding automation or AI-assisted coding tools;
* Experience developing or improving analytical reporting systems;
* Knowledge of GMP requirements and pharmaceutical manufacturing processes;
* Experience with matrix leadership, project coordination, or stakeholder negotiation.


**Benefits**  

* Health insurance with dental and vision insurance options.
* Holiday pay.
* 401(k) program.
* Employee referral bonus program.
* The client retains the right to hire the contractor directly.

##### **About Peraton**

Peraton is a next-generation national security company that drives missions of consequence spanning the globe and extending to the farthest reaches of the galaxy. As the world’s leading mission capability integrator and transformative enterprise IT provider, we deliver trusted, highly differentiated solutions and technologies to protect our nation and allies. Peraton operates at the critical nexus between traditional and nontraditional threats across all domains: land, sea, space, air, and cyberspace. The company serves as a valued partner to essential government agencies and supports every branch of the U.S. armed forces. Each day, our employees solve the most daunting challenges that our customers face. Visit peraton.com to learn how we’re keeping people around the world safe and secure.

##### **About The Role**

Peraton is seeking a mid-level **Data Scientist** to help analyze and resolve key questions related to key issues of national security facing the United States. The data scientist will contribute to intelligence production and support the creation of internal capabilities to enhance and enable the effectiveness of analytic teams. The ideal candidate has experience supporting the Intelligence Community (IC), strong attention to detail and time management skills, and the ability to perform independently and within a team in a fast‑paced environment.



**Key Responsibilities** of this role include:

* Analyzing data collect and recommending opportunities to automate processes;
* Collaborating with internal and external partners to support the development of data collect strategies and opportunities to enhance that collect;
* Supporting the ingest, use, and management of data while ensuring all activity adheres to applicable customer and community standards;
* Maintaining quality standards as directed by the program leadership team and supporting the implementation of corrective actions as needed;
* Engaging with colleagues to support initiatives designed to enhance customer tools and close capabilities gaps


\*\*\*\*This is contingent upon contract award\*\*\*\*



#MissionIntel

